  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PADEO Workshops Tunisia: Youth employment in horticulture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of PADEO is to co-create a Dutch development approach (vision, strategy and action plan) that positively impacts youth employment in Tunisia, based on insights from local workshops in which the key local stakeholders, including where possible also &#x201C;unusual&#x201D; suspects (the ones often forgotten, e.g. youth representatives, actors that are already changing the game), have been actively engaged. PADEO (Programmatic Approach Sustainable Economic Development) is a pilot program (besides Tunisia also for Uganda, Kenya, Ghana and Sudan) initiated by the Directorate-General for International Cooperation of the Dutch government (Sustainable Economic Development Department (DDE)). The pilot program focuses on applying a new systems approach to achieving progress on SDG 8.The PADEO pilot in Tunisia focuses on stimulating youth employment in the agrifood sector by making working in agriculture attractive again for youth.In this project, the consultant is requested to facilitate four workshops with the aim of designing an approach and activities oriented to have as much impact as possible on tackling youth employment.Two workshops will be multi-stakeholder workshops and two workshop will be with the pilot team. The workshops will build further upon the systems study of the Challenge Fund for Youth Employment. Specific focus should lie on involving youth and women, identifying local needs and what could be the added value of Dutch expertise and clearly identifying opportunities for interventions from the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
